    "created_at": "2021-11-18T16:59:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-11-18T16:59:25Z",
    "body": "The Bash start-up scripts and the various configuration knobs are notoriously free form.  There's no guarantee which file will be called in which order and how many times.  It can all change from one OS distribution to another.  :)\r\n\r\nIf Starship manages to set the `PS1` before `toolbox.sh` gets to it, then I think the diamond or hexagon indicator should get prefixed automatically, but I don't know if that will adversely affect the prompt.  However, that won't happen if Starship gets to it later.\r\n\r\nI am wondering if `toolbox.sh` should detect that there's a Starship-controlled prompt in place, and leave it alone.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
